  not hidden, at the path its own row gives, plus the site pages that are
  not doors. /services and the landing page already read that rule. A static
  file cannot import it, so this is that list written out. The durable
  writer belongs next to scripts/build-llms.ts, which already computes the
  same set for llms.txt.

  HIDDEN WHILE THE LINKEDIN APPLICATION IS UNDER REVIEW: hidden doors are
  omitted. Delete the hidden flags when the application is answered and
  rewrite this file from that list.

  Two kinds of address are absent on purpose.

  - Partner and hidden doors. A sitemap is a public list of URLs handed to
    crawlers, so an omitted offer listed here is a published offer. A
    robots.txt Disallow line would print the same address just as publicly.
    Leaving those addresses out is the only entry that does not publish them.
  - /w/:token. A workspace token is a bearer credential that lives in the
    URL, and listing one would publish the credential.
-->
